# For PCBs designed using KiCad: http://www.kicad-pcb.org/
# Format documentation: http://kicad-pcb.org/help/file-formats/

# Temporary files
*.000
*.bak
*.bck
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*~
_autosave-*
*.tmp
# NOT ignored: KiCad 5 symbol cache and rescue libraries.
#
# Upstream ignored these, which is why midi-solenoid-driver-cache.lib is absent
# from this repository and the schematic reports a missing library on open. It
# is harmless here because every symbol in this design comes from a stock KiCad
# library, so a current KiCad resolves them all -- but a project using any
# custom symbol would be unrecoverable this way. Keep the cache committed.
#*-cache.lib
#*-rescue.lib
*-save.pro
*-save.kicad_pcb

# Netlist files (exported from Eeschema)
*.net

# Autorouter files (exported from Pcbnew)
*.dsn
*.ses

# Exported BOM files
*.xml
*.csv

# KiCad editor lock files and automatic project backups.
# These appear whenever the project is open in KiCad and are never source.
*.lck
~*.lck
*-backups/

# Python tooling under tools/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc

# Arranger outputs are derived from a song and organ.yaml; regenerate, do not commit.
*.organ.mid
*.organ.txt

# Tune sources are not committed (they are other people's music); their plans are.
tools/organ-arranger/tunes/*.mid
